From f2e2f49ca6ae1d269a97ebcde149ed3bcfd16de0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julius Brussee <juliusbrussee@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 7 May 2026 17:57:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cavemem: invert search.alpha Zod docstring (upstream bug #25)

Cherry-picked from upstream JuliusBrussee/cavemem@f2e2f49 (the issue-sweep
commit that lives on `main` and is bundled into the unreleased v0.3.0 via
the changesets release PR #31). Only the schema-docstring portion of that
commit is extracted here.

Upstream bug:    #25 (search.alpha description is inverted)
Source PR:       #31  https://github.com/JuliusBrussee/cavemem/pull/31
Source commit:   f2e2f49ca6ae1d269a97ebcde149ed3bcfd16de0
Source file(s):  packages/config/src/schema.ts

What this patch does (paraphrasing the upstream changeset entry):

  config (#25): Correct the inverted description for `search.alpha`. The
  ranker computes `alpha * bm25 + (1 - alpha) * cosine`, so `1 = pure
  BM25` and `0 = pure cosine`. Doc-only — no behavior change.

This is a one-line .describe() string change to the Zod settings schema
(`packages/config/src/schema.ts`). The default value (0.5) and the
runtime ranker behavior are unchanged. The docstring is what
`cavemem config show` prints and what the smoke-test in this integration
asserts on (Requirement 9.AC3).

Verified to apply cleanly with `patch -p1` and `git apply --check`
against the v0.2.1 source tarball
(https://api.github.com/repos/JuliusBrussee/cavemem/tarball/v0.2.1).

The unrelated parts of f2e2f49 (musl detection, claude-code installer,
codex installer, opencode installer, test updates) are NOT included
here. The opencode installer fix is split out into the sibling patch
cavemem-14-hook-payload-shape.patch.
---
 packages/config/src/schema.ts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/packages/config/src/schema.ts b/packages/config/src/schema.ts
index be8e0de..f791f61 100644
--- a/packages/config/src/schema.ts
+++ b/packages/config/src/schema.ts
@@ -83,7 +83,7 @@ export const SettingsSchema = z
           .min(0)
           .max(1)
           .default(0.5)
-          .describe('Hybrid rank weight: 0 = pure BM25, 1 = pure cosine, 0.5 = balanced.'),
+          .describe('Hybrid rank weight: 1 = pure BM25, 0 = pure cosine, 0.5 = balanced.'),
         defaultLimit: z
           .number()
           .int()
